THOUGHT: NullAway still flags `node.id` as nullable even with the inline null check, likely due to its flow analysis limitations in this compact `if` form. I should refactor the loops into clearer blocks where the null check and dereference are separated, which NullAway can understand better.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '397,401c\	    if (ignoreCase) {
	      for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
	        node = nodes.get(i);
	        if (node.id != null && node.id.equalsIgnoreCase(id)) return node;
	      }
	    } else {
	      for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
	        node = nodes.get(i);
	        if (node.id != null && node.id.equals(id)) return node;
	      }
	    }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/model/Node.java
```

